course: dictionary
lesson: 1805
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Cloudy means with many clouds in the sky, so the sun is hidden. The words around it give you the clue. «You can't get burnt when it's cloudy» tells you the sun is hidden, so it cannot burn your skin.
explain: Cloudy can also mean not clear. «Cloudy water» is water you cannot see through, so it may have dirt in it. Swap in the word murky and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Cloudy can even describe the mind. «Cloudy memories» are memories that are not clear. The same word has three meanings, so always look at the other words to find the right one.
fact: Cloudy means with many clouds in the sky, so the sun is hidden.
fact: Cloudy water is not clear and may contain dirt or germs, so it should not be drunk.
fact: Weather forecasts use the words "cloudy", "partly cloudy" and "overcast".
fact: On a cloudy day a sundial tells nothing at all, because it needs the sun to show the time.
fact: The adjective changes its form: cloudy, cloudier, cloudiest.
exercise: «You can't get burnt when it's cloudy,» says your sister. What does cloudy mean here? | *With many clouds, so the sun is hidden | Shiny like new glass | Full of rain that falls fast | Very hot and bright
exercise: Which phrase describes water you should not drink? | *cloudy water | sunny day | cool breeze | clear sky
exercise: «On a cloudy day it tells nothing at all.» What does cloudy show about the sun? | The sun is shining brightly | *The sun is hidden by clouds | The sun has set for good | The sun is too hot to see
test: «The cataract made the lens inside her eye cloudy.» What does cloudy mean here? | *Not clear, so she could not see well | Very cold and frosty | Covered in sunshine | Shiny and bright
test: Which phrase is a weather forecast word? | curt | *partly cloudy | famished | heartbroken
exam: Which sentence uses cloudy to mean not clear in the mind? | The day is cloudy and grey | The water in the pond is cloudy | The sky is cloudy this morning | *Her memories of the holiday are cloudy
